arriving to a sea of press but worlds  away from the red carpet reception kevin  spacey is used to rather than fans  clamoring for autographs photographers  fighting to get a shot of the double  oscar winner walking into court this a  rare public appearance since his career  and conduct has come under scrutiny over  the last five years  the hearing brief confirmation that the  charges relate to alleged sexual  assaults which took place in 2005 and  2013 the 2008 charge had claimed he  caused a man to engage in penetrative  sexual activity without consent  spacey wasn't asked to enter a plea but  in response to the cps arguing that he  shouldn't be allowed to fly home his  lawyers argued that he wasn't a flight  risk that he'd voluntarily submitted to  four days worth of questioning by met  police in new york that he strenuously  denied the charges but understands that  he needs to respond to them in order to  move on with his life  all of the alleged incidents occurred  within the time frame when spacey was  based in the uk as artistic director of  the old vic theatre  i know what you want we've seen little  of him aside from a cryptic house of  cards-esque video posted onto social  media since the metropolitan police  announced its investigation the decision  by the cps to charge the hollywood  a-lister follows a review of that  evidence  a hugely connected figure in the arts in  both america and the uk  spacey's lawyer said he denies any and  all criminality and in a statement last  month the actor said he was confident he  could prove his innocence  granted unconditional bail his next  hearing is at southern crown court in  july casey spencer sky news
 

